    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup is anchored by the dual-threat speed of **Corbin Carroll** and **James Wood**, both of whom present as elite daily plays with scores of 77.46 and 72.41, respectively. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a favorable matchup against Kumar Rocker, where his dynamic platoon advantage and projected #5 slot drive his ceiling. Meanwhile, **James Wood** is set to lead off against Ure\u00f1a; his elite 0.415 xwOBA, combined with the favorable park factor and a weak opposing arm, positions him as our most reliable catalyst for runs and stolen bases. **Trevor Story** and **Brice Turang** also maintain strong efficiency scores near 68, with **Trevor Story** specifically exploiting the 4.58 xERA of Dobnak to mitigate his usual volatility.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Austin Riley**, who narrowly missed our starting threshold with a score of 42.69. While his base projection is solid, the matchup against Tim Mayza forced a significant 18% downward adjustment for the opposing pitcher's skill, compounded by the detrimental impact of a #7 lineup spot. **Max Muncy** remains the lowest-ranked starter at 49.03; his inclusion is purely a function of roster depth, as he struggles against Bryan Woo\u2019s 3.53 xERA. We remain cautious regarding **Griffin Conine**, whose score of 40.08 barely clears our floor; starting him against Glasnow is a high-risk move, though his platoon edge provides just enough justification to keep him active to chase HR volume.\n\nWe are actively monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Cole Young**, **Brice Turang**, **Max Muncy**, **Corbin Carroll**, and **Josh Naylor**. Any shift in their assigned batting order could trigger a re-optimization, particularly for **Cole Young**, whose current score is sensitive to his placement at the bottom of the order. While the data suggests a productive day for our core, the presence of Glasnow on the opposing mound for **Griffin Conine** serves as the primary danger to our overall efficiency, and we will watch the pre-game weather reports for any signs of restricted offensive production.",
